title: Dashboard › Payers at a glance › Read the table and pick a payer
route: /dashboard?payer=harborview
intro: The last card on the page. One row per payer, plus a totals row. A click on a payer row narrows the whole page to that payer; a second click clears it. The payer's name and 'Open Payers' lead to the Payers page. A link from Ask FLO scrolls the card into view.
dir: TD
---
start s1 "Scroll to 'Payers at a glance'"
start s2 "Follow 'Open Dashboard, By payer' in Ask FLO\nThe address is /dashboard?focus=payers"
process f1 "Page scrolls to the card\nThe card is outlined in green for about 2 seconds\nThe ?focus part is then removed from the address"
screen sc1 "Card header\n'Payers at a glance'\n'Waiting now, how long decisions take, and how often they go your way. Click a row to narrow everything on this page.'\nOn the right: 'Open Payers'"
decision d0 "Is Program or Request type set?"
toast t0 "Sentence added to the header\n'Waiting counts follow your Program and Request type filters.'"

group gCols "Columns and rows"
  screen r1 "Payer\nName, e.g. 'Cardinal Health Plan', as a link, and its kind: 'Medicaid plan', 'Commercial', 'Medicare Advantage', 'Carve-out'"
  screen r2 "Waiting\nRequests Received or Under review at that payer\nFollows Program and Request type, not Payer, Stage or dates"
  screen r3 "Decision time\n'2.8 d' and 'typical 2 d'\nOchre when the average is over 15 percent above typical"
  screen r4 "Approved as asked\n'63%' with a small bar\nGreen at 80 and above, ochre below"
  screen r5 "Denied (30 d) and Info asks (30 d)\nCounts that rescale with the date range; the heading shows the number of days"
  screen r6 "Reached by\n'Portal', 'Phone', 'Fax' or 'Portal and fax'"
  screen r7 "Row order\nCardinal Health Plan, Summit Medicaid HMO, Beacon PPO, Harborview MA, Lakeshore Behavioral, Evergreen"
  screen r8 "Last row 'All payers'\nSums of Waiting, Denied and Info asks; '-' elsewhere; not clickable"
endgroup

click c1 "Click a payer row (not its name)\nOr Tab to the row and press Enter or Space"
decision d1 "Is that payer already selected? (row tinted green)"
process p1 "Payer filter set to that payer"
process p2 "Payer filter goes back to 'All payers'"
store w1 "Filter 'payer'"
process p3 "Address gets ?payer=harborview, or loses it\nTable goes back to its first 8 rows"
screen sc2 "Page follows the payer\nHeadline 'Harborview MA: 3 waiting, taking 3.1 days.'\nTile counts and the requests table follow it; the Payer menu shows its name"
screen sc3 "Payers table keeps all six rows\nThe chosen row is tinted green and marked selected\nWaiting counts do not change"

click c2 "Click the payer's name, e.g. 'Harborview MA'\nThe filter does not change"
click c3 "Click 'Open Payers'"
process n2 "Address becomes /payers/harborview\nA new history entry, so Back returns here"
process n3 "Address becomes /payers"
goto g4 "Continues in: Payers › Arrive on the page"
goto g1 "Continues in: Dashboard › Headline › What the headline and sub line say"
goto g2 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Date range shortcuts, keys and the address"
goto g3 "Continues in: Dashboard › Filters › Payer, Program, Request type and Stage"
goto g5 "Continues in: Global shell › Top bar › Ask FLO › What FLO answers"

s1 --> sc1 --> d0
s2 --> f1 --> sc1
s2 -.-> g5
d0 -->|Yes| t0 --> r1
d0 -->|No| r1
r1 --> r2 --> r3 --> r4 --> r5 --> r6 --> r7 --> r8
r5 -.-> g2
r8 --> c1
c1 --> d1
d1 -->|No| p1 --> w1
d1 -->|Yes| p2 --> w1
w1 --> p3
p3 --> sc2 --> g1
p3 --> sc3
sc3 -.-> g3
r1 --> c2 --> n2 --> g4
sc1 --> c3 --> n3 --> g4
